{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed development would appear incongruous within its setting and harmful to the character of the area, as a result of its uncharacteristic and unduly large lightwells and the visual clutter associated with the proposed safety railings surrounding these. The application also leaves insufficient scope for high-quality soft landscaping to the front of the site. The proposal is therefore contrary to the intentions of the National Planning Policy Framework which seeks to promote high quality design, London Plan policies D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach), D4 (Delivering good design) and Local Plan policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture) and SC4 (Scale and density of new housing development).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal, by reason of poor outlook, a failure to demonstrate sufficient sunlight and daylight levels, a lack of usable high-quality private amenity space and substandard bedrooms sizes which fail to comply with the Nationally Described Space Standards, would result in inadequate living conditions for future occupiers of the development. The proposal is therefore contrary to London Plan policies D4 (Delivering good design), D5 (Inclusive Design) and D6 (Housing quality and standards) and Local Plan policies SC3 (Meeting the need for a mix of housing size and type), SC4 (Scale and density of new housing development) and SC5 (Ensuring suitable internal and external space)."
  ],
